525	<h2 id="build-script">10. The build_cpp.sh Helper</h2>
526	
527	<p>The script wraps the CMake workflow into a single command and handles the most common failure mode: a Python without development headers.</p>
528	
529	<div class="file-label">scripts/build_cpp.sh — key logic</div>
530	<pre><span class="cmt"># 1. Find a Python with dev headers (prefer uv-managed)</span>
531	INCLUDE_DIR=$($PYTHON -c <span class="str">"import sysconfig; print(sysconfig.get_path('include'))"</span>)
532	[ -f <span class="str">"$INCLUDE_DIR/Python.h"</span> ] || { echo <span class="str">"ERROR: Python.h not found"</span>; exit <span class="num">1</span>; }
533	
534	<span class="cmt"># 2. Find pybind11 cmake config from pip</span>
535	PYBIND11_CMAKE=$($PYTHON -c <span class="str">"import pybind11; print(pybind11.get_cmake_dir())"</span> <span class="num">2</span>/dev/null || <span class="kw">true</span>)
536	
537	<span class="cmt"># 3. Configure — pass Python and pybind11 paths explicitly</span>
538	cmake -S <span class="str">"$REPO_ROOT"</span> -B <span class="str">"$BUILD_DIR"</span> \
539	    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
540	    -DPython3_EXECUTABLE=<span class="str">"$PYTHON"</span> \
541	    -DCMAKE_LIBRARY_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY=<span class="str">"$REPO_ROOT/src/oil_alpha"</span> \
542	    <span class="str">"${CMAKE_EXTRA_ARGS[@]}"</span>
543	
544	<span class="cmt"># 4. Build in parallel</span>
545	cmake --build <span class="str">"$BUILD_DIR"</span> --parallel $(nproc)</pre>
546	
547	<p><code>-DCMAKE_LIBRARY_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY</code> redirects the <code>.so</code> file directly into <code>src/oil_alpha/</code>. That means after the build, <code>PYTHONPATH=src python -c "import oil_volume_cpp"</code> works immediately — no install step needed.</p>
